WEBVTT

00:07.160 --> 00:10.480
Weakness is a sin.

00:32.439 --> 00:34.039
That hurts.

01:28.280 --> 01:29.519
Will you beg for mercy?

01:31.799 --> 01:32.760
That's good.

01:33.079 --> 01:35.959
Your strength is the only thing
worth believing in.

01:36.400 --> 01:39.959
If you desire fangs
that are sharp enough to kill,

01:40.359 --> 01:41.480
then come with me.

03:41.840 --> 03:44.159
Jesus. Again
with the energy drink.

03:44.240 --> 03:46.800
How do you stomach that crap
first thing in the morning?

03:47.960 --> 03:49.159
No, thanks.

03:49.840 --> 03:51.000
It'll help you wake up.

03:55.360 --> 03:59.000
This tastes just like that nasty-ass cold
medicine I had to drink as a kid.

03:59.599 --> 04:02.360
You know, that sweet, syrupy kind that
makes you want to throw up?

04:07.639 --> 04:10.199
- Holy crap, was that a laugh?
- You're imagining things.

04:10.280 --> 04:12.560
No, no, I saw you smile.
Come on, let's see it again.

04:12.639 --> 04:15.599
- You need to get your eyes checked.
- There's no need to be shy, Ducky-poo.

04:15.680 --> 04:18.199
One more smile.
Come on now. Don't ignore me.

04:18.279 --> 04:19.560
Like I said...

04:23.279 --> 04:25.800
Listen, Ducky, this place
is too desolate for her grave.

04:26.560 --> 04:28.480
We got to make sure
she doesn't feel lonely.

04:29.879 --> 04:31.759
So after we're done taking
care of business,

04:31.839 --> 04:34.720
go and give her a proper burial, okay?
Back in her hometown.

04:35.920 --> 04:40.480
Ninjas like us, we don't have
hometowns or even gravestones.

04:41.680 --> 04:44.120
We're just left to rot away
as nameless corpses.

04:47.519 --> 04:49.480
It's the fate
that awaits us all.

04:50.560 --> 04:53.600
Let's make this the place
where she can rest in peace,

04:53.680 --> 04:55.759
near the people
she considered family.

04:56.560 --> 04:57.680
Sure.

04:59.680 --> 05:04.319
We'll make sure that her soul finds peace
by putting an end to all of this.

05:05.759 --> 05:07.360
I'll hunt down Yamaji.

05:07.800 --> 05:09.920
He's the source,
the center of everything.

05:10.319 --> 05:13.680
Eliminating him is the only way
to dismantle the organization.

05:14.319 --> 05:15.759
I'll make sure to take care of AUZA.

05:16.480 --> 05:18.879
We got our hands on solid
evidence of their corruption,

05:19.680 --> 05:23.000
and once we leak that data to the media
outlets, it'll become a feeding frenzy.

05:23.639 --> 05:25.240
She gave her life for that info,

05:25.920 --> 05:27.879
so there's no way
I'm letting it go to waste.

05:28.800 --> 05:33.839
I really hate to ruin the mood, but,
unfortunately, we've got big trouble here.

05:35.279 --> 05:36.759
So, like, all of the data we nabbed,

05:37.079 --> 05:41.199
it was encoded by a frigging genius,
and unless we crack it,

05:41.680 --> 05:42.920
nobody is going to be able
to see any of it.

05:43.000 --> 05:45.040
God damn it. So it's all locked up?

05:45.560 --> 05:46.800
Was that AUZA's doing?

05:47.199 --> 05:50.360
Nope. Looks like the one who took it
is the person who encrypted it.

05:50.439 --> 05:52.759
- You mean Emma?
- Yeah.

05:52.839 --> 05:55.959
She obviously wanted to make sure that
it stayed safe no matter what happened.

05:56.040 --> 05:58.439
At least until she passed it off
directly to you.

06:00.680 --> 06:04.240
Hate to tell you, all of her forethought
came back to bite us in the ass,

06:04.319 --> 06:06.879
because now we got to solve
this stupid-ass puzzle.

06:06.959 --> 06:08.160
If we want to take
a look at the data.

06:09.199 --> 06:10.839
- Can you do it?
- Maybe.

06:10.920 --> 06:12.480
First step is analyzing the algorithm

06:12.560 --> 06:14.560
to figure out what type
of encryption method she used.

06:16.800 --> 06:17.720
Wait a sec.

06:18.439 --> 06:20.240
<i>Reports are coming in that
a facility being built by AUZA</i>

06:20.319 --> 06:21.959
<i>has been hit
by a terrorist attack.</i>

06:22.639 --> 06:23.639
Officials have said it's likely

06:23.720 --> 06:25.480
<i>that extremist members
of an ecological group</i>

06:25.560 --> 06:27.399
<i>pushing for more
environmental protections</i>

06:27.480 --> 06:28.720
<i>are the ones responsible
for the crime.</i>

06:31.519 --> 06:33.199
Are you satisfied now?

06:33.839 --> 06:36.600
Mr. Secretary, my company is the victim
of an unjust terrorist attack.

06:36.680 --> 06:39.040
The explosion was no accident.

06:39.439 --> 06:40.759
Allow me to once again guarantee you

06:40.839 --> 06:42.519
that our facilities are 100% safe
and secure.

06:42.600 --> 06:45.160
<i>And you simply expect me
to believe that?</i>

06:45.240 --> 06:46.439
Yeah, obviously.

06:47.240 --> 06:49.120
I mean, public opinion
is going to be on our side.

06:49.199 --> 06:51.639
I've already had a friendly chat with all
the members of the advisory committee

06:51.720 --> 06:55.040
that you were so concerned about,
and they had no problems with it.

06:56.279 --> 07:00.279
<i>And I suppose that you had a similar
friendly chat with the press, too.</i>

07:03.839 --> 07:07.399
In any case, there's no problem now that
we've cleared up our misunderstanding.

07:07.720 --> 07:10.879
Let's get back to working together
and making those power plants a reality.

07:11.199 --> 07:12.199
What do you say?

07:12.279 --> 07:15.040
We can all have a hand in reinventing
the world of tomorrow.

07:16.199 --> 07:17.519
I will not rush my decision.

07:17.959 --> 07:21.639
<i>You still haven't convinced me that the
power plants are as safe as you claim.</i>

07:22.360 --> 07:26.600
<i>And, further, if you end up having
trouble like this a second time,</i>

07:27.079 --> 07:29.519
<i>we're going to be forced
to reconsider the plan itself.</i>

07:30.000 --> 07:32.439
<i>I strongly suggest
that you keep that in mind.</i>

07:33.800 --> 07:35.160
<i>Also, while I have
your attention,</i>

07:35.519 --> 07:38.160
<i>I suggest that you learn
to end your conversations</i>

07:38.240 --> 07:39.600
in a less reprehensible way.

07:39.680 --> 07:42.319
<i>Otherwise, you won't be
making any friends.</i>

07:43.519 --> 07:45.319
I appreciate the good advice.

07:47.079 --> 07:48.120
Brainless turd.

07:48.199 --> 07:51.920
Just shut the hell up and do
what I say, God damn it.

07:54.680 --> 07:57.199
Excuse me, sir.
Apparently, someone's hacked us.

07:57.519 --> 08:00.399
It seems they were able to gain access
to the company's main server.

08:00.879 --> 08:01.879
What the hell?

08:01.959 --> 08:06.199
It's possible some of our top-secret data
that was stored there has been stolen.

08:07.120 --> 08:08.519
Damn it to hell!

08:10.120 --> 08:14.800
Why can't anything just go
how I want it to?

08:18.920 --> 08:20.480
Things are not looking good, sir.

08:21.519 --> 08:23.279
We've already obtained all the
development data on the reactor

08:23.360 --> 08:24.360
and the Gusoku gear.

08:24.920 --> 08:28.160
It shouldn't be difficult for us to
establish our own production line.

08:33.279 --> 08:35.720
Damn it. I can't believe it.
They beat us to the punch.

08:35.799 --> 08:37.559
It's a waste of time to leak
anything to the press now.

08:38.120 --> 08:41.279
Yeah, AUZA probably has every
outlet in their pocket already.

08:41.600 --> 08:44.440
Journalism my ass.
The bigger the scandal,

08:44.519 --> 08:46.440
the greater the bribes and corruption
that they profit from.

08:46.919 --> 08:49.720
I know. We could try finding
independent media outlets

08:49.799 --> 08:51.320
that are still willing
to come out against them.

08:51.399 --> 08:53.320
- What do you think?
- That won't work.

08:53.399 --> 08:55.960
Corporal's already have way
too much of an advantage.

08:56.039 --> 08:57.679
We can't leak anything
to the press.

08:58.000 --> 09:00.360
We'll just end up getting screwed over
by media manipulation.

09:00.440 --> 09:03.320
We need a platform that we know
for sure will boost our message.

09:04.600 --> 09:06.440
Why don't we put it on ChikTak?

09:06.519 --> 09:10.600
We can easily rack up to 3 million views
if it goes viral. Here's the plan.

09:10.679 --> 09:14.799
We display the AUZA data over footage
of a busty bombshell flaunting her chest.

09:15.840 --> 09:17.320
Hey, calm down.
I have an idea that might work.

09:17.799 --> 09:19.799
You keep working
on cracking that encryption.

09:20.159 --> 09:21.639
Wait. Where are you going?

09:25.720 --> 09:27.080
It's a frigging crow.

09:28.600 --> 09:29.559
What's that thing in its mouth?

09:37.600 --> 09:39.080
A challenge. To a duel.

09:39.159 --> 09:40.159
You're going to fight a crow?

09:41.639 --> 09:47.960
The ninja code is what unites us, what
keeps us safe, and what allows us to live.

09:48.519 --> 09:52.679
Therefore, we must also meet
our end by the ninja code.

09:53.159 --> 09:56.200
Therefore, we must also meet
our end by the ninja code.

09:57.039 --> 09:58.200
The ninja?

09:59.039 --> 10:01.559
The name of the
strongest warrior known to man.

10:02.039 --> 10:04.399
And whoever stands
at the helm of the ninjas

10:04.919 --> 10:08.039
is someone with enough power
to rule over the entire world.

10:08.919 --> 10:11.519
The power to rule over the world?

10:18.519 --> 10:20.279
I surrender.

10:27.679 --> 10:30.879
That's enough.
You've already won.

10:34.080 --> 10:37.480
Weaklings like this have
no right to be here.

10:38.039 --> 10:40.759
This man is not a weakling.
He's a ninja, just like us.

10:41.320 --> 10:42.919
- Just like us?
- Yes.

10:43.440 --> 10:45.639
A comrade who fights with us
to defend Japan.

10:46.080 --> 10:48.279
Anyone who proves unfit
should be cast aside.

10:48.840 --> 10:51.120
Choosing to cover
for them leads to death.

10:51.919 --> 10:54.080
Nobody survives by fighting alone.

10:55.440 --> 10:57.200
It seems like you two
have differing opinions.

10:57.639 --> 11:00.039
There's an easy way to prove
which one of you is correct.

11:00.120 --> 11:01.720
You should both just fight it out.

11:03.080 --> 11:04.879
That's the ninja way, isn't it?

11:08.240 --> 11:09.320
Fine by me.

11:17.639 --> 11:18.639
That ends it.

11:19.200 --> 11:20.240
Looks like we have a draw.

11:23.159 --> 11:24.080
You're very good.

11:36.279 --> 11:39.919
Despite how mean you are to everyone,
you sure are really nice to the crows.

11:40.720 --> 11:42.000
You're not so scary after all.

11:43.159 --> 11:46.200
"The Reaper."
That's what they call you, you know?

11:46.279 --> 11:48.320
Every single trainee who ended
up fighting you lost their nerve

11:48.399 --> 11:50.080
and gave up on their teachings.

11:50.840 --> 11:53.080
There was one exception, though.

11:53.840 --> 11:55.159
What's the deal with that guy?

11:56.200 --> 11:58.519
I guess you're interested
in more than just crows, huh?

11:59.039 --> 12:00.960
You'll learn more about him,
whether you like it or not.

12:01.039 --> 12:03.080
After all, we'll all be training
to become ninjas together.

12:15.240 --> 12:18.399
Those who successfully passed
the latest examination are...

12:20.600 --> 12:22.000
just these three.

12:23.679 --> 12:26.120
I shall now assign a mission
for you all to complete.

12:27.039 --> 12:28.559
And should you
complete it successfully,

12:28.639 --> 12:31.279
then you shall be honored
with the title of ninja.

12:37.960 --> 12:39.440
We got what we came for.

12:39.519 --> 12:42.080
Now we just need to bring it
back with us. Let's hurry.

12:48.919 --> 12:49.840
Wait.

12:54.399 --> 12:56.720
Reinforcements.
They got here fast.

12:56.799 --> 12:58.279
Someone must have
leaked our plans.

12:58.639 --> 13:00.000
This is the only road out.

13:00.519 --> 13:02.159
It's only a matter of time
until they find us.

13:02.519 --> 13:04.120
- Out of my way.
- Hey.

13:04.600 --> 13:06.080
Are you going to try
and hold them off by yourself?

13:26.759 --> 13:28.159
Goddamn freak!

13:47.440 --> 13:49.000
Those who are weak die.

13:55.000 --> 13:56.039
That's...

13:57.720 --> 13:59.039
just how it goes.

14:07.080 --> 14:09.679
Hey. Hey. Come on.

14:11.039 --> 14:12.200
Snap out of it.

14:13.879 --> 14:15.000
It's you.

14:19.200 --> 14:20.120
Hurry.

14:23.279 --> 14:24.360
Cover my back.

15:06.480 --> 15:07.879
That's all I have to report.

15:09.120 --> 15:10.879
You did this to test them, didn't you?

15:11.360 --> 15:13.120
We only seek the strongest.

15:16.440 --> 15:17.600
Why did you come back?

15:18.559 --> 15:20.240
Your priority should have
been finishing your mission.

15:20.960 --> 15:22.759
Correct.
We did exactly what was necessary

15:22.840 --> 15:24.799
to ensure the operation would be
completed.

15:26.080 --> 15:27.320
There's no doubt you're strong,

15:28.679 --> 15:32.120
but with the three of us united, it makes
us capable of much greater things.

15:32.919 --> 15:36.279
You're not alone.
You should keep that in mind.

15:45.360 --> 15:48.399
I was abandoned by both
my parents after I was born.

15:51.799 --> 15:53.919
They left me alone to die
and rot on a mountain,

15:54.399 --> 15:56.879
but the crows fed me
and kept me alive.

15:58.840 --> 16:00.279
Now I only have faith
in two things:

16:01.039 --> 16:02.120
the crows that saved me
and my own strength.

16:04.720 --> 16:06.879
I've never let anyone
cover my back before.

16:09.559 --> 16:10.679
That was new for me.

16:11.720 --> 16:13.879
If I accompany you two,
will I see new horizons?

16:16.039 --> 16:17.120
Is that possible?

16:45.200 --> 16:48.919
Why are you doing this?

16:50.360 --> 16:51.919
Because we both broke the code.

16:57.200 --> 16:58.159
But we made a pact...

16:59.080 --> 17:00.759
to put our lives
in each other's hands,

17:01.759 --> 17:02.960
to journey together.

17:05.079 --> 17:06.240
I'm sorry.

17:06.799 --> 17:08.960
Fine, then.
You better kill me now.

17:11.039 --> 17:12.079
Because if you don't,

17:13.680 --> 17:15.839
I will be the one
who hunts you both down.

17:31.799 --> 17:33.960
Higan! Mari!

17:58.599 --> 18:00.240
This place is spooky as hell.

18:02.359 --> 18:04.119
Yeah, this is where we used to
hide out a long time ago.

18:04.799 --> 18:06.519
He's already here.
I can sense it.

18:06.599 --> 18:08.839
Aw, man. You should have just ignored
his request for a duel.

18:08.920 --> 18:10.400
Why did we even bother
coming here?

18:11.000 --> 18:13.640
Because he's part of the past
that I left behind.

18:14.279 --> 18:16.640
And I can't move forward
without facing my past.

18:24.920 --> 18:26.920
Exiled ninjas must face death.

18:28.680 --> 18:32.680
I told you before that a time might come
when we would fight each other.

18:33.960 --> 18:36.400
And now here we are.

18:38.000 --> 18:38.920
Zai.

18:50.039 --> 18:52.680
- What the hell, Mike?
- Crazy stuff. Huh?

18:53.079 --> 18:55.880
One of your agents on the verge of
retirement suddenly becomes a terrorist.

18:56.559 --> 18:59.920
- Let's take this somewhere private.
- Emma's dead, just FYI.

19:00.759 --> 19:01.680
Oh, really?

19:02.440 --> 19:03.480
But it was thanks to her

19:03.559 --> 19:05.960
that I got my hands on evidence of
AUZA's dirty deeds.

19:06.599 --> 19:09.599
She was true to her duty until the end,
unlike some people I know.

19:10.880 --> 19:12.640
You, on the other hand,
are AUZA's lapdog.

19:13.720 --> 19:15.640
The good news is, I don't think
they bothered to buy off

19:15.720 --> 19:17.000
every single person in the FBI.

19:17.440 --> 19:20.680
I bet there's some honest agents left
who wouldn't take that dirty money.

19:22.000 --> 19:23.880
And since you got
connections to AUZA,

19:24.799 --> 19:26.559
you must know
who those agents are.

19:27.400 --> 19:29.240
- Get to the point already.
- It's simple.

19:29.839 --> 19:31.799
I want you to give the evidence
that Emma found to them.

19:33.319 --> 19:35.119
I have no idea what you're talking about.

19:35.680 --> 19:37.839
It sounds to me like
you've gone stark raving mad.

19:38.319 --> 19:41.519
Besides, there's no good reason for me
to give in to your demands.

19:42.039 --> 19:45.319
Listen, I'm not here to file
a report with my superior.

19:45.640 --> 19:49.480
I'm here to talk with my partner. He used
to care when people broke the law.

19:49.559 --> 19:51.880
Our duty is to protect honest citizens
from law-breaking criminals.

19:52.480 --> 19:53.759
Sound familiar?

19:53.839 --> 19:56.960
Those are the exact words
you told me when we first met.

19:58.839 --> 20:01.720
Isn't that right, partner?

20:04.480 --> 20:08.119
I don't recall saying that.
That was a very long time ago.

20:09.079 --> 20:11.839
I just found Mike now.
Get over here on the double.

20:11.920 --> 20:12.839
Asshole.

20:49.960 --> 20:52.160
You can forget about
using your stupid tricks.

20:52.240 --> 20:54.240
Just come at me
with everything you have.

21:46.359 --> 21:49.559
You really should have killed me
when you had the chance.

21:50.279 --> 21:52.640
You are the embodiment
of my mistakes,

21:53.039 --> 21:56.319
and now I'm going to use your
blood to wash my past clean.

21:56.920 --> 21:59.160
I have a duty,
something I must see through,

21:59.640 --> 22:01.240
and I cannot die
until it's finished.

22:02.039 --> 22:06.000
Then let's rid each other
of our burdens once and for all.

22:10.000 --> 22:14.920
Revised and Synchronized by
FAST TITLES MEDIA
